📦 Setup Instructions
1. Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/klaviyo-ai-campaign-bot.git
cd klaviyo-ai-campaign-bot
2. Install Docker Desktop

Download and install Docker Desktop:
https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/

3. Create Persistent n8n Volume
docker volume create n8n_data
4. Start ngrok

Install ngrok:
https://ngrok.com/download

Authenticate ngrok:

ngrok config add-authtoken YOUR_NGROK_TOKEN

Start tunnel:

ngrok http 5678

Copy the HTTPS forwarding URL.

Example:

https://abcd-1234.ngrok-free.app
5. Start n8n

Replace the ngrok URL below with your own:

docker run -it --rm --name n8n -p 5678:5678 -e WEBHOOK_URL=https://YOUR_NGROK_URL -e N8N_HOST=YOUR_NGROK_HOST -e N8N_PROTOCOL=https -v n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n
6. Open n8n

Open:

https://YOUR_NGROK_URL
7. Import Workflow
Open n8n
Click “Import from File”
Select the exported workflow JSON
8. Configure Credentials

Add the following credentials inside n8n:

Telegram Bot
Create bot using @BotFather
Add Telegram API credential
Google Gemini API
Add Gemini API key credential
Klaviyo API
Add Header Auth credential
Include Klaviyo private API key
9. Activate Workflow

Enable the Telegram Trigger workflow.

Send a message to your Telegram bot to test the automation.

🔒 Security Notes

Do NOT commit:

API keys
Telegram bot tokens
ngrok tokens
.env files

Use environment variables or n8n credential manager instead.

